```typescript
return (...args: any[]) => {
    if (timer !== null) {
        clearTimeout(timer);
    }
    timer = setTimeout(() => {
        timer = null;
        fn(...args);
    }, waitMs);
};
```

The closure captures the latest `args`, so the final call passes through the latest arguments. The file keeps the original export signature `export function debounce(fn: (...args: any[]) => void, waitMs: number)` and includes a self-test that runs under `node debounce.ts` (using `node:assert` + a direct `import.meta.url` check) and prints `all tests passed`.
